value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30dfc837-d5c1-5761-8aca-09d8e183f2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575033} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8dd47c6-0daf-57eb-b7fa-e36f8f40c1d7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8bf0613-dc2d-57fb-b4e9-45d51faad202" :question/math-academy-id "q-348682" :question/problem "Given that $r(t)=⟨cos\\,\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{4}{t-1}⟩,$ what is $|r(3)|?$\n\n$|r(3)|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the function at $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨cos\\,\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{4}{3-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(3)| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e550028-3605-535d-afc4-0b67b596e1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574997} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd5b5cd-005e-5343-bec2-584e99c95568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575117} {:answer/id #uuid "6969e4a1-4a1e-5a38-83f0-7effe12a76ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575136} {:answer/id #uuid "cef7cdb8-1750-586d-9b65-5c0a924fd3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575315} {:answer/id #uuid "f6712659-f7f2-5848-8213-91e6b729c7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e550028-3605-535d-afc4-0b67b596e1d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574997} :answer-field/id #uuid "760957fd-b385-5f58-b025-bc8ecf6a9ef0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f479be92-cf45-5de7-9956-484ec8fcce81" :question/math-academy-id "q-161508" :question/problem "What is the value of $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\right) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576